{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A maskil of Asaph. Why, O Elohim, have You forsaken</b> — the word משכיל is the beginning of a piyyut, and this psalm is on that same account." "<b>למה</b> — paʿul." "<b>זנחת — the flock</b>, because anger is likened to fire, therefore it is called Your anger [אפך]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 74, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:22.734582644Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}